+The Menu Style asset's Skin gives every part its own art per state (Normal, Hovered, Focused, Pressed, Selected, Disabled - each a texture, a material or an SVG), drawn instead of the built-in shapes; parts left empty keep the built-in look. Parts: Row, FocusBar, ModifiedDot, SectionHeading, CategoryHeading, TabBar, Tab, TabIndicator, SwitchTrack, SwitchKnob, SliderTrack, SliderFill (cut at the value, never squashed), SliderThumb, SelectorBox, SelectorArrow (drawn pointing left; the right one is it turned round), Pip, Segment, Dropdown, DropdownArrow, KeySlot, PrimaryButton, SecondaryButton, GhostButton, FooterPrompt, SearchBox, DescriptionPanel, Footer, DialogCard, ListCard, ListOption, Scrim, ScrollThumb, ScrollTrack. Per part: Tint With Palette (a white image takes the palette's colour for that state), Tint, Outset (grow past the part: glows, frames), Keep Built In. A material gets its own instance per part with live scalars Hover, Focus (0..1 eased), Pressed, Selected, Disabled, Value (slider / switch 0..1, selector option 0..1), Time, Width, Height and vectors PaletteColor, Accent - one material (build_ui_material) can draw every state. In create_settings_menu: skin {Row: "<material path>", SliderThumb: {normal: "<svg>", pressed: "<svg>"}, Tab: {normal: "<mi>", selected: "<mi>", tint_with_palette: true}}; later: set_asset on the style, Style.Skin.<Part>.Normal = {ImageSource: "Texture", Image: "<path>"} (or ImageSource "SVG", SVG "<path>").
+Layout and type for the look: TitleAlignment / TabsAlignment (HAlign_Left, HAlign_Center), TabPadding, ButtonPadding, SwitchSize, SliderTrackHeight, SliderThumbSize, SelectorArrowSize, PipHeight, DialogWidth, ScrollBarThickness, bUppercaseTabs / bUppercaseSections / bUppercaseLabels / bUppercaseButtons, fonts with LetterSpacing.
+Your own UMG parts (Style.Widgets; create_settings_menu widgets {tab, heading, footer_prompt, description, search, dialog, option_list}): Widget Blueprints of MenuTabWidget (On Tab Assigned / On Tab State Changed, Select Tab; LabelText filled), MenuHeadingWidget, MenuFooterPromptWidget (On Glyph Changed for the device's key, Press), MenuDescriptionWidget (On Description Changed; TitleText, ValueLineText, BodyText, OptionText, WarningText, NoteText filled), MenuSearchWidget (an EditableText named SearchText), MenuDialogWidget (On Dialog Shown, Choose(index), Get Dialog Focus Widget), MenuOptionListWidget (On Option List Shown, Pick Option). The screen keeps doing the work (input, focus, sounds, narration). Rows and controls by rule: Style.Widgets.Rules [{Part Row | Control, SettingIds (wildcards "Video.*"), Sections, Pages, Kind, ChoiceDisplay (Selector / Dropdown / Buttons), WidgetClass}] - a MenuSettingRowWidget (the whole row) or a MenuSettingControlWidget (only the control, in the built-in row); either gets On Row State Changed (hovered, focused, pressed, enabled, modified, waiting for a key), On Row Stepped (left / right), On Row Activated, Get Menu Style / Palette, and stays one of the screen's rows (focus, description, narration, sounds).
